{
  "_doc": [
    "Declared authority for every registered REST route. RouteAuthorityTest walks the live",
    "registry and fails when a route is missing here, when this file names a route the code",
    "no longer registers, and when the declared callback is not the one actually registered.",
    "A new route therefore cannot ship without someone stating who may reach it.",
    "",
    "audience: public = anyone including signed out | member = any logged-in user |",
    "owner = the object owner (or an admin) | admin = a capability holder |",
    "guarded = a controller callback that resolves authority itself.",
    "",
    "A public route MUST carry a reason recording how it was verified, not a claim that it",
    "is safe. A public route that takes an object id MUST say what stops it leaking a record",
    "its caller may not see.",
    "",
    "Ownership is resolved by the file of the class that REGISTERS the route, so a Pro",
    "controller inheriting a Free base-class guard is still recorded here in Pro."
  ],
  "routes": {
    "DELETE /wpss/v1/auth/devices/(?P<device_id>[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+)": {
      "audience": "guarded",
      "permission_callback": "WPSellServices\\API\\AuthController::check_permissions",
      "object_id": true,
      "writes": true
    },
    "DELETE /wpss/v1/auth/sessions/(?P<uuid>[a-zA-Z0-9\\-]+)": {
